# Public port for the local server. Point Cloudflare Tunnel to this port.
PORT=8080
# SQLite file path. Defaults to wearsic.db in the server directory.
WEARSIC_DB_PATH=wearsic.db
# Optional shared key. Configure the same key in Wearsic Settings.
# `wearsic cloudflare` creates one here if this is empty; an existing value
# is never replaced.
WEARSIC_API_KEY=
# Optional authenticated YouTube browser cookie string for bot-challenged server IPs.
# Never commit a real cookie. Example format: SID=...; HSID=...; SSID=...
WEARSIC_YOUTUBE_COOKIE=
# Self-healing engine updates (default on). When YouTube breaks the extraction
# engine, the server downloads the newest release ZIP, verifies it, stages it,
# and run-termux.sh applies it on restart. Set to 0 to update manually only.
WEARSIC_AUTO_UPDATE=1
# Directory for staged updates + update.json. Default: wearsic-state/ next to the DB.
#WEARSIC_STATE_DIR=
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare front door (`wearsic cloudflare`) — a PERMANENT public URL.
#
# A Cloudflare Quick Tunnel alone gives a random https://<random>.trycloudflare.com
# that changes on every restart, so a watch can never remember it. The front
# door puts a Cloudflare Worker in front of the tunnel: the Worker lives at a
# fixed https://<worker>.<subdomain>.workers.dev address and is re-pointed at
# the new tunnel hostname whenever the tunnel changes. No domain, no cost.
#
# Easiest setup (one command; fills in a key only if the one above is blank):
#   wearsic cloudflare
# It starts the engine, creates WEARSIC_API_KEY if needed, walks through
# Cloudflare auth, installs cloudflared, deploys, verifies, and prints the
# permanent URL + API key together for the watch.
#
# Optional pre-authorization (saves the credential for you):
#   wearsic cloudflare login
# That uses wrangler's browser/device OAuth when wrangler is installed. If
# npm is present but wrangler is not, it offers a one-time install; otherwise
# it prompts for a scoped API token with hidden input and saves it here (mode
# 600). You can also put credentials in this file or the environment.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN   optional when you use `wearsic cloudflare login` or
#                        have a wrangler OAuth session. Otherwise a Cloudflare
#                        API token with "Workers Scripts: Edit" and
#                        "Account Settings: Read" (Workers & Pages → API
#                        Tokens → Create Token). Never the Global API Key.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID  optional — auto-detected from the token (or
#                        `wrangler whoami --json`) and persisted. Set it only
#                        when the credential can see multiple accounts.
# CLOUDFLARE_SUBDOMAIN   optional — your workers.dev subdomain. An existing
#                        one is reused and saved; it is created only when the
#                        account has none.
# CLOUDFLARE_WORKER      optional — the Worker name, default "wearsic".
#                        It becomes a DNS label, so letters/digits/dashes only.
#
# A public URL REQUIRES WEARSIC_API_KEY above — without one the engine would
# be open to anyone who guesses the address. The one-command setup creates a
# key only when this is blank; it never replaces a key you already chose.
#
# After setup, verify the real proxied audio path (not just /health):
#   wearsic cloudflare status
#   wearsic cloudflare verify
#   wearsic cloudflare logs
# To also probe a real track through the permanent URL:
#   WEARSIC_CF_PLAYBACK_ID=<videoId> wearsic cloudflare verify
#CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
#CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
#CLOUDFLARE_SUBDOMAIN=
#CLOUDFLARE_WORKER=wearsic
